    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the empire thrives on law, order, and sophisticated societal structures, the tribes of the Depths are governed by instinct and the basic principles of tribal survival—'till we gather or be gathered by others.' Over this simple and brutal axiom, they have adapted complex customs worthy of admiration from a more ruthless, primordial perspective:\n\nIn the Depths, the concept of property barely exists. Resources must be exploited to sustain the tribe, and shared access to these resources reinforces a kind of unity and camaraderie. When a member of a tribe fails to contribute to its survival efforts due to illness, aging, or even as a consequence of war, it is not uncommon to see the tribe embracing this member once recovered, or shouldering the responsibility to care for the wounded, demonstrating deep-rooted value for communal welfare—albeit one far less centered around individual achievement.\n\nLaw, as the empire knows it, does not hold the same significance. Disputes are often resolved by the Dark Shaman or through tribal consensus, drawing upon ancient, likely hereditary wisdom, passed down through tales and blood-lines. Violations of this deeper wisdom are punished, but these societies lack a formalized legal framework.\n\nTheir understanding of individual life is intertwined with the concept",
